 "summary": "Definition bodies are unexposed (no `@[expose]`) with `(rfl)`-proved `_def` lemmas, and each of the four structure functions carries a complete characteristic API \u2014 summed form, unit-norm and `V = 1` specialisations, quark/antiquark separation with one-sided row/column variants, charge conjugation, positivity, and the \u00b1 combinations Layer 3 consumes. Simp annotations sit only on normal forms and cannot be blocked (`Matrix.one_apply` is not simp upstream); the generic matrix lemmas are public in the `Matrix` namespace, and no compatibility, private-infrastructure, or duplicate surface is introduced.",
